.TH MINNI 1 "October 2026" "minni" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
minni \- control the minni clipboard daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minni
.RI [ --socket " path" ]
.RI [ --json ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show daemon, capture, and history state.
.TP
.B list
List history. Accepts --limit, --cursor, and --pinned.
.TP
.BI search " query"
Search text, labels, MIME types, and source applications.
.TP
.BI show " id"
Show item metadata.
.TP
.BI preview " id"
Create and return a private bounded image preview.
.TP
.BI export " id --output path"
Export original item bytes without overwriting an existing file.
.TP
.BI copy " id"
Restore an item to CLIPBOARD. Use --selection primary for PRIMARY.
.TP
.BI pin|unpin|remove " id"
Mutate one stable item ID.
.TP
.B clear --unpinned|--all
Clear the requested history scope.
.TP
.B pause|resume
Control capture.
.TP
.B watch
Print events and reconnect after daemon restarts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 succeeds; 2 is invalid usage; 3 means daemon unavailable; 4 means an item
was not found; 5 is a limit or stale cursor; 1 is another failure.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Wayland is not supported.
